  "caveats": [
    "The identity sum_lambda f^lambda s_lambda = p_1^n is a CLASSICAL theorem of symmetric-function theory (Macdonald I.7; Stanley EC2 section 7), cited rather than re-proved. This probe verifies it numerically at the substrate specialisation; the Lean file YLambdaNormalizationSign.lean carries it as an explicit hypothesis (hZ) and proves the sign consequence sorry-free. The premise is established literature, NOT a conjecture."
